    <h1>Security</h1>
    <p class="ld-sub">A high-level view of how we protect information and the systems behind our work.</p>
    <div class="ld-meta">Last updated: June 2026</div>
  </header>
  <article class="ld-body">
<section><h2><span class="n">01</span>Secure infrastructure</h2><p>Our website and systems run on reputable, secure infrastructure, and all traffic is served over <strong>HTTPS</strong> with encryption in transit.</p></section>
<section><h2><span class="n">02</span>Protecting data</h2><p>We apply access controls and the principle of least privilege so that information is only available to those who need it, and we follow internal security practices designed to keep client and company data protected.</p></section>
<section><h2><span class="n">03</span>Continuous improvement</h2><p>Security is never finished. We review and improve our practices on an ongoing basis as technology and risks evolve.</p></section>
<section><h2><span class="n">04</span>A note on detail</h2><p>To protect their effectiveness, we do not publish the technical specifics of our security implementation. For security-related inquiries, contact <a class="inl" href="mailto:hello@basecampstudio.pk">hello@basecampstudio.pk</a>.</p></section>
  </article>
